<div class="prose-club">
  <p><em>Last updated: {{ "2026-10-10" | dateMedium }}</em></p>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>This website is run by Penn Golf Club Limited, Penn Common, Penn, Wolverhampton {{ site.address.postcode }}. If you have any questions about this notice or your data, contact us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> or on {{ site.phone }}.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect personal information that you choose to give us, for example when you:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>send an enquiry (contact, membership, society, wedding, party, meeting or sponsorship forms)</li>
    <li>subscribe to our email newsletter</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This usually means your name, email address, phone number and the details of your enquiry. We use it only to respond to you and, if you subscribed, to send our newsletter. You can unsubscribe at any time.</p>
  <p>Form submissions are processed and stored by our website host, Netlify, Inc., on our behalf.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This website does not use advertising or analytics cookies. Some features store small amounts of information in your browser's local storage, such as your digital scorecard and Handicap Index, so they are still there next time you visit. This information never leaves your device, and you can clear it at any time through your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Weather forecasts</strong> are loaded from Open-Meteo. No personal information is sent.</li>
    <li><strong>Maps</strong> are provided by OpenStreetMap.</li>
    <li><strong>Fonts</strong> are served by Google Fonts.</li>
    <li><strong>Tee time and competition booking</strong> is provided by BRS Golf, and the <strong>Members' Hub</strong> by Club Systems. These have their own privacy policies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, and to object to how we use it. To make a request, contact us using the details above. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>).</p>
</div>
